Programmatic vocabulary corpus for javelin-steno TypeScript expansion, never enumerated into a flat dict. Unlike dict.steno, this file defines types and @count construct families whose stroke space is too large to materialize — the function family alone covers 0..15 parameters via the AOEU count bank, yielding 16 shape strokes instead of T^16 rows. `build-javelin` compiles two small tables (types + constructs) into a C++ header; StenoGeneratedDictionary replays the append walk per lookup to generate expansions on demand.

Core vocabulary is docs/steno-format.md plus %T (D11), the fuse-target type slot that marks where the return type is merged into the construct stroke (docs/pipeline.md, "The reference walker"). All types nest unbounded (D8) — a generic's %t argument may itself be any type to any depth, unlike dict.steno's Pass B which restricts arity-0 pools. 

The type table defines 18 base types (number, string, boolean, etc.) and 6 generics: Promise<%t>, Map/Record<%t,%t>, Set<%t>, Array<%t>, Error, Generator<%t>. The type emitter STKWR-T is the differential test pin — shallow enough that expand_dict can enumerate its pool-depth subset for walker-vs-pipeline validation.

The function family STKWR-PBGS has 10 variants (deFauLT, aRrow Typed, aRrow with newline, Method, asyNc, yeilD, iiFe, consRuCTor, SeT) all @count AOEU @fuse. Fuse fixes fill order (D12): return slot %T is stroked first, then parameters %0..%d in template order. The IIFE variant uses %(d+1) to emit args after the body.